{"id":"028aa154996383db","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-cor-cohen-adds.md","title":"Cohen Add Corollary","display":"cor-cohen-adds — Cohen Add Corollary","type":"corollary","metadata":{"type":"corollary","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-cor-cohen-adds","aliases":["58-cor-cohen-adds"],"display":"cor-cohen-adds — Cohen Add Corollary","depends_on":["[[58-df-cohen]]","[[58-df-cardinal]]","[[58-df-ctm]]","[[58-df-forcing-relation]]","[[58-df-zfc-check-name]]","[[58-df-formula]]","[[58-df-free-variable]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"corollary"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-cor-cohen-adds"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-cor-cohen-adds</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"cor-cohen-adds — Cohen Add Corollary"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"aa69e82627a80f1e\" href=\"?note=aa69e82627a80f1e\" title=\"58-df-cohen\">58-df-cohen</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"58-df-cardinal\">58-df-cardinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"66d43bb76d055059\" href=\"?note=66d43bb76d055059\" title=\"58-df-ctm\">58-df-ctm</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"46b2495f214783c3\" href=\"?note=46b2495f214783c3\" title=\"58-df-forcing-relation\">58-df-forcing-relation</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"d29823616dbc5931\" href=\"?note=d29823616dbc5931\" title=\"58-df-zfc-check-name\">58-df-zfc-check-name</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"58-df-formula\">58-df-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"715a32e91161b34f\" href=\"?note=715a32e91161b34f\" title=\"58-df-free-variable\">58-df-free-variable</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Explicit relation signatures used below: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CTM}_S\\subseteq V^{2}\">\\(\\mathrm{CTM}_S\\subseteq V^{2}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\subseteq V^{1}\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\subseteq V^{1}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CheckName}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\mathrm{CheckName}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cohen}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\mathrm{Cohen}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\subseteq V^{6}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\subseteq V^{6}\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,\\Gamma,P,\\leq_P,1_P,\\lambda,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Cohen}}\\in V\">\\(M,\\Gamma,P,\\leq_P,1_P,\\lambda,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Cohen}}\\in V\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\">\\(\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P,\\lambda\\in M\">\\(P,\\lambda\\in M\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"66d43bb76d055059\" href=\"?note=66d43bb76d055059\" title=\"58-df-ctm\">58-df-ctm</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\lambda)\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\lambda)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"58-df-cardinal\">58-df-cardinal</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cohen}_S(P,\\leq_P,\\lambda)\">\\(\\mathrm{Cohen}_S(P,\\leq_P,\\lambda)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"aa69e82627a80f1e\" href=\"?note=aa69e82627a80f1e\" title=\"58-df-cohen\">58-df-cohen</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Cohen}}\">\\(\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Cohen}}\\)</span> is a three-free-variable formula code expressing “<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v_0=\\omega_1\">\\(v_0=\\omega_1\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|\\mathcal P(v_1)|\\geq v_2\">\\(|\\mathcal P(v_1)|\\geq v_2\\)</span>”</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CheckName}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{CheckName}_S\\)</span> are the registered forcing relation and canonical-name predicates</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}cohen\\text{-}adds}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\\land P,\\lambda\\in M\n\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\lambda)\\land\\aleph_1^M\\leq\\lambda\n\\land\\mathrm{Cohen}_S(P,\\leq_P,\\lambda)\\land1_P=\\varnothing\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Cohen}}\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)\n\\land\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}(\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Cohen}})=\\{v_0,v_1,v_2\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\exists\\widehat{\\omega_1^M},\\widehat\\omega,\\widehat\\lambda\\in M\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{CheckName}_S(\\widehat{\\omega_1^M},\\omega_1^M,P)\n\\land\\mathrm{CheckName}_S(\\widehat\\omega,\\omega,P)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{75pt}\\land\\mathrm{CheckName}_S(\\widehat\\lambda,\\lambda,P)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\!\\left(\nM,1_P,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Cohen}},\n\\langle\\widehat{\\omega_1^M},\\widehat\\omega,\\widehat\\lambda\\rangle,P,\\leq_P\n\\right)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}cohen\\text{-}adds}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\\land P,\\lambda\\in M\n\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\lambda)\\land\\aleph_1^M\\leq\\lambda\n\\land\\mathrm{Cohen}_S(P,\\leq_P,\\lambda)\\land1_P=\\varnothing\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Cohen}}\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)\n\\land\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}(\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Cohen}})=\\{v_0,v_1,v_2\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\exists\\widehat{\\omega_1^M},\\widehat\\omega,\\widehat\\lambda\\in M\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{CheckName}_S(\\widehat{\\omega_1^M},\\omega_1^M,P)\n\\land\\mathrm{CheckName}_S(\\widehat\\omega,\\omega,P)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{75pt}\\land\\mathrm{CheckName}_S(\\widehat\\lambda,\\lambda,P)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\!\\left(\nM,1_P,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{Cohen}},\n\\langle\\widehat{\\omega_1^M},\\widehat\\omega,\\widehat\\lambda\\rangle,P,\\leq_P\n\\right)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The ccc preserves <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega_1\">\\(\\omega_1\\)</span>, and the <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span> coordinates yield an injection of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\check\\lambda\">\\(\\check\\lambda\\)</span> into the extension's reals.  The conclusion now passes a formula code and an explicit tuple of three canonical names to the six-place forcing relation.</li>\n<li>The conclusion <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"2^{\\aleph_0}=\\aleph_2\">\\(2^{\\aleph_0}=\\aleph_2\\)</span> additionally requires <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda=\\aleph_2\">\\(\\lambda=\\aleph_2\\)</span> and a ground-model continuum bound.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-cohen","status":"resolved","id":"aa69e82627a80f1e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cohen]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"5fb1c2241d1943d1","a